Description: list the stereo picture types in Showfoto's desktop entry
 MPO, JPS and PNS are sub-classes of JPEG and PNG (kimageformats-stereo.xml
 in kf6-kimageformats). Showfoto already opens them (stereo-layer.patch adds
 jps, mpo and pns to its file filters and shows the pair in 3D). The edition
 makes Gwenview their default (/etc/xdg/kde-mimeapps.list in
 sparky-stereo-look); naming them in the desktop entry makes Open With and the
 list of applications offer Showfoto for these types directly instead of by
 inheritance only.
 digiKam's own entry (org.kde.digikam.desktop) names no MIME type and its
 command line takes no file, so it is not listed there.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/core/showfoto/main/org.kde.showfoto.desktop
+++ b/core/showfoto/main/org.kde.showfoto.desktop
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@
 Exec=showfoto -qwindowtitle %c %U
 Icon=showfoto
 Type=Application
-MimeType=image/gif;image/x-xpixmap;image/x-xbitmap;image/jpeg;image/png;image/tiff;image/x-bmp;image/x-psd;image/x-portable-bitmap;image/x-portable-pixmap;image/x-portable-graymap;image/x-dcraw;image/heif;image/heic;
+MimeType=image/gif;image/x-xpixmap;image/x-xbitmap;image/jpeg;image/png;image/tiff;image/x-bmp;image/x-psd;image/x-portable-bitmap;image/x-portable-pixmap;image/x-portable-graymap;image/x-dcraw;image/heif;image/heic;image/x-jps;image/x-mpo;image/x-pns;
 Terminal=false
 Categories=Qt;Graphics;Photography;
 X-DocPath=showfoto/index.html
